# Intermediates are large and fully rebuildable with `make demo`: the raw
# ČÚZK tiles (~5 GB per region), float rasters, MBTiles, reprojected copies.
# NOTE: Config.out_dir resolves relative to the CONFIG FILE's directory, so
# configs/north.yaml writes under configs/data_north/ — covered below.
data/
data_north/
configs/data_*/

# The tile archives are served from S3, not from this repo. PMTiles is read
# with HTTP range requests, which any object store answers directly, so the
# 100 MB per-file ceiling that forced one archive per region was a GitHub
# constraint only — it does not apply to S3. National coverage is ~17 GB and
# ~161 regions, which no git repo should carry. Set TILE_BASE in index.html
# to the bucket or CDN origin; "./" keeps web/serve.py working locally.
web/*.pmtiles

# JPL ephemeris kernel, ~16 MB, fetched on demand into data/.
de421.bsp

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Personal photos carry GPS EXIF (exact home coordinates). This repo is wired
# to GitHub Pages, so anything committed here becomes public. Delete these two
# lines if you want them tracked.
photos/
